; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Follow the Leader
; CATEGORY: Animation & Many Turtles
; LEVEL:    Intermediate
; TAGS:     many turtles, TOWARDS, ASK, chasing, trails
; SUMMARY:  A leader turtle wanders about and a line of turtles follows, each one chasing the turtle ahead.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Turtle 0 is the leader. It wanders around, turning a little at
;   random. Turtle 1 always turns to face the leader and steps
;   toward it. Turtle 2 chases turtle 1, turtle 3 chases turtle 2,
;   and so on. Each follower draws a faint colored trail, so you
;   see the curves they make as they cut corners.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run and watch the chase. Press Stop to end it.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * ASK to read another turtle's position: ASK 2 [POS]
;   * TOWARDS to face a point
;   * keeping followers from bunching up with a distance test
;   * a chain of turtles, each one following the next
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Make all the followers chase the leader directly.
;   * Make the followers faster than the leader. What happens?
;   * Let the leader follow the mouse with MOUSEPOS.
; ============================================================

make "colors [[220 60 60] [240 150 40] [230 210 50] [70 180 90] [60 140 230] [150 90 220]]

; SETUP places all the turtles in a row and gives them colors.
to setup
  ask 0 [penup setxy 0 0 setshape "turtle setpencolor [40 40 40] showturtle]
  for [k 1 6] [
    ask :k [
      penup setxy -40 * :k 0 setheading 90
      setshape "arrow
      setpencolor item :k :colors
      setpensize 2
      showturtle
      pendown
    ]
  ]
end

; LEAD moves the leader: a random wiggle, and a turn back toward the
; middle if it wanders too close to an edge.
to lead
  ask 0 [
    right (random -15 15)
    if (distance [0 0]) > 250 [setheading towards [0 0]]
    forward 5
  ]
end

; FOLLOW moves turtle :k toward the turtle in front of it, but only
; while it is more than 30 steps behind, so they do not pile up.
to follow :k
  localmake "target ask :k - 1 [pos]
  ask :k [
    setheading towards :target
    if (distance :target) > 30 [forward 4.5]
  ]
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [250 248 240]
setup
make "frame 0
forever [
  lead
  for [k 1 6] [follow :k]
  ; Wipe the old trails now and then so the picture stays tidy.
  make "frame :frame + 1
  if 0 = remainder :frame 900 [clean]
  wait 1
]
